A||||8||fierospeeder||3.1 HP??||||1||
Z||000000||fierospeeder||03-04-2000||01:11 AM||||I thought about switching the engines in my 4 banger to the 2.8 or something with six cylinders.<P>I have recently gone to the junkyard a lot, but the only thing is the one i go to doesn't have any fieros.  One day i was just walking around and looked at the buicks and chevys for v6.  Im not sure but it looks like a 1990 caviler or some small car but the intake says 3.1 on it.  Does anyone know what the HP is on this engine that came originally as a 3.1?<BR>I want to do the 3800 but its to much money and i would have to buy kits to actually do it unless swapping the cradle will work.||||reg||1
Z||000001||87GT||03-04-2000||01:17 AM||||My 94 Grand Prix SE I had came with a 3.1 V6 and it was rated at 160hp.  160 with that car was not enough.  It was kinda sluggish.  Nice looking car though. It was bright white, 2-door, fin, it was really cool.  But, I liked my fiero more.. hahha||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||03-04-2000||01:48 AM||||I know someone who had a Z-24 Cavalier and the spec sheet said it was rated at 150hp. I think the rating of 150 to 160 was dependant on the car The larger cars were set at 160 the cav's and sunbird were at 150. To make a 3.1L out of a 2.8L you just need crank and rods. I think IRM use to sell a kit to convert a Fiero 2.8L to a 3.1L and they boasted 165hp. I'm not sure if any block work had to be done to do this.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||03-04-2000||04:51 AM||||Are you sure that the only difference between the 2.8 and the 3.1 is the crank and rods?  Not doubting you, but I'm about to get the bottom end of my new GT rebuilt and it would be nice to upgrade to a 3.1 for about the same amount of $$.  Got any part #s for the new/different parts???  Are they any more expensive than the stock parts???||||reg||1
Z||000004||Phaeton||03-04-2000||04:57 AM||||I think crank and pistons was meant.  Shorter rods would eat into high rpm performance.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||03-04-2000||06:29 AM||||Oh.  Thanx.  What would the price difference be between a stock rebuild and a 2.8 into a 3.1 rebuild?  What about a 2.8 into a 3.2 rebuild?||||reg||1
Z||000006||Phil||03-04-2000||07:39 AM||||Monkey to rebuild your 85 into a 3.1 you will also need a different flywheel/flex plate. When I had my 2.8 rebuilt the difference in the cranks was $25||||reg||1
Z||000007||batboy||03-04-2000||10:00 AM||||The 3.1 engine that Fierospeeder is seeing in those FWD GM cars has aluminum heads. These heads are a good design, but you have to use pistons and the intake manifold that goes with the heads. These engines can be swapped into the fiero, but you'll need the donor car's ECM and engine wiring harness. Some of the accessories like A/C compressor or alternator might have to be changed to fit, I don't know. These are DIS engines that used a serpentine belt.<P>Changing a 2.8 cast iron headed engine into a 3.1 with cast iron heads (like was used in some early 90's FWD mini-vans) is fairly easily done. Use a 3.1 crank, 3.1 pistons made for the cast iron heads, and a neutrally balanced flywheel. Tada, you just made a 3.1 and if you bore it out, it's a 3.2 liter.<P>Go to this link for more info. The 2.8 to 3.1 conversions are discussed towards the bottom of the page, the top part is about 3.4 swaps.<P><BR><A HREF="http://members.yourlink.net/dragon/parks/e-conv.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://members.yourlink.net/dragon/parks/e-conv.htm</A> <p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 03-04-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||fierospeeder||03-04-2000||10:45 AM||||I thought about just putting in the 3.1 from another car because it would be easier, except the wire harness part.  I would know from start im getting that 160hp and i can always bore it over and or port and polish.  Im also running without AC so i dont have that problem.||||reg||1
